@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 Alarm 清除、幂等、消息分叉与 Edge 传播

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam ArrowColor #111827
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #111827
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActorBorderColor #111827
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #111827
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam QueueBorderColor #111827
skinparam QueueBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam NoteBorderColor #92400E
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #374151
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F9FAFB
skinparam BoxBorderColor #4B5563
skinparam BoxBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

actor "REST Client" as Client
box "Application / REST" #EFF6FF
participant "AlarmController" as Controller
participant "DefaultTbAlarmService" as App
participant "DefaultTbAlarmCommentService" as Comment
participant "EntityActionService" as Action
end box

box "Alarm application service" #ECFDF5
participant "DefaultAlarmSubscriptionService" as Subscription
participant "SubscriptionManager\nWebSocket" as WS
participant "AlarmTriggerProcessor" as Notification
end box

box "DAO" #F8FAFC
participant "BaseAlarmService" as Service
participant "JpaAlarmDao\nAlarmRepository" as Dao
participant "EdgeEventSourcingListener" as EdgeEvent
end box

database "PostgreSQL\nalarm / entity_alarm\nalarm_comment / audit_log" as PG
queue "Rule Engine Queue" as RuleQueue
participant "RuleNodeActor" as Actor
participant "TbClearAlarmNode" as ClearNode
participant "TbDeviceProfileNode\nDeviceState / AlarmState" as Profile

== REST first clear ==
Client -> Controller: POST /api/alarm/{id}/clear
activate Controller
Controller -> Controller: checkAlarmId(id, WRITE)
Controller -> App: clear(alarm, currentUser)
activate App
App -> Subscription: clearAlarm(tenant,id,now,null)
activate Subscription
Subscription -> Service: clearAlarm(...)
activate Service
Service -> Dao: clearAlarm(...)
activate Dao
Dao -> PG: SELECT clear_alarm(tenant,id,ts,NULL)
activate PG
PG -> PG: SELECT alarm FOR UPDATE
alt row exists and cleared=false
  PG -> PG: UPDATE cleared=true, clear_ts=ts
  PG --> Dao: success=true, cleared=true, alarm_info
else row exists and already cleared
  PG --> Dao: success=true, cleared=false, current alarm_info
else row missing or tenant mismatch
  PG --> Dao: success=false
end
deactivate PG
Dao -> Dao: toAlarmApiResult\nmodified = created || cleared || modified
Dao --> Service: AlarmApiCallResult
deactivate Dao

alt result contains Alarm
  Service -> PG: read existing entity_alarm targets\nwhen propagation flags are enabled
  Service -> EdgeEvent: publish ActionEntityEvent(ALARM_CLEAR)
  activate EdgeEvent
  EdgeEvent -> RuleQueue: Core/Edge notification, callback null
  EdgeEvent --> Service: listener catches its own failures
  deactivate EdgeEvent
end
Service --> Subscription: result + propagated entities
deactivate Service

alt first clear: successful && modified
  Subscription -> Subscription: schedule AlarmUpdateCallback\non wsCallBackExecutor
  Subscription --> App: return without waiting
  deactivate Subscription

  ... asynchronous callback may run before or after REST side effects ...
  Subscription -> WS: onAlarmUpdate per propagated entity\nlocal or Core Queue
  Subscription -> Notification: process AlarmTrigger(CLEARED)

  App -> Comment: save SYSTEM comment subtype CLEAR
  activate Comment
  Comment -> PG: INSERT alarm_comment partition
  Comment -> Action: log ADDED_COMMENT
  Action -> RuleQueue: COMMENT_CREATED
  Action -> Notification: AlarmCommentTrigger
  Action -> PG: async audit_log ADDED_COMMENT
  Comment --> App: saved comment
  deactivate Comment

  App -> Action: logEntityAction(ALARM_CLEAR)
  activate Action
  Action -> RuleQueue: push TbMsgType.ALARM_CLEAR\noriginator is Alarm originator
  Action -> PG: async audit_log ALARM_CLEAR
  note right of Action
  processNotificationRules has no ALARM_CLEAR case,
  so it does not emit EntityActionTrigger.
  end note
  Action --> App: returns without waiting for consume/audit
  deactivate Action
  App --> Controller: cleared AlarmInfo
  Controller --> Client: HTTP 200
else duplicate clear
  Subscription --> App: modified=false; skip WS/AlarmTrigger
  deactivate Subscription
  App --> Controller: ThingsboardException already cleared
  Controller --> Client: HTTP 400
  note over Client,EdgeEvent
  The Edge ActionEntityEvent was published in BaseAlarmService
  before DefaultTbAlarmService rejected the duplicate.
  end note
else missing row after controller check
  Subscription --> App: success=false
  deactivate Subscription
  App --> Controller: ITEM_NOT_FOUND
  Controller --> Client: error response
end
deactivate App
deactivate Controller

note over PG,RuleQueue
The alarm row, comments, audit, WebSocket, notification,
Rule Engine messages and Edge events do not share one transaction.
end note

== Explicit Clear Alarm Rule Node ==
RuleQueue -> Actor: input TbMsg
activate Actor
Actor -> ClearNode: onMsg(ctx,msg)
activate ClearNode
alt msg originator type is ALARM
  ClearNode -> Subscription: findAlarmById(AlarmId)
else other originator
  ClearNode -> Subscription: findLatestActiveByOriginatorAndType(...)
end
Subscription -> Service: DAO query
Service -> PG: SELECT Alarm
PG --> Service: Alarm or null
Service --> Subscription: Alarm or null
Subscription --> ClearNode: Alarm or null

alt missing or already cleared at pre-query
  ClearNode -> Actor: tellNext(False)
else active Alarm
  ClearNode -> ClearNode: async JS/TBEL details\nmetadata includes prevAlarmDetails
  ClearNode -> Subscription: clearAlarm(...,details)
  Subscription -> Service: same clear path
  Service -> PG: clear_alarm(...)
  PG --> Service: result
  Service --> Subscription: result + Edge event
  Subscription --> ClearNode: result; WS/AlarmTrigger scheduled if first
  alt result.isCleared
    ClearNode -> RuleQueue: enqueue root ALARM_CLEAR action message
    alt producer success
      RuleQueue --> ClearNode: onSuccess
      ClearNode -> Actor: tellNext(ALARM, Cleared)\nisClearedAlarm=true
    else producer failure
      RuleQueue --> ClearNode: onFailure
      ClearNode -> Actor: tellFailure(transformed ALARM)
    end
  else race produced no-op
    ClearNode -> Actor: tellSuccess(original message)
  end
end
deactivate ClearNode
deactivate Actor

note over ClearNode,PG
The database is already committed before root action enqueue.
A producer failure cannot restore the active Alarm.
end note

== Device Profile automatic clear ==
RuleQueue -> Actor: telemetry / attributes / activity\nor periodic self message
activate Actor
Actor -> Profile: onMsg(ctx,msg)
activate Profile
Profile -> Profile: update/read latest snapshot\nevaluate create rules by severity
alt no create rule TRUE and currentAlarm + clear rule exist
  Profile -> Profile: evaluate clear condition
  alt clear condition TRUE
    Profile -> Profile: reset create and clear rule state
    Profile -> Subscription: clearAlarm(...,createDetails(clearState))
    Subscription -> Service: same persistence path
    Service -> PG: clear_alarm(...)
    PG --> Service: result
    Service --> Subscription: result + Edge event
    Subscription --> Profile: result; async WS/AlarmTrigger on first clear
    opt result.isCleared
      Profile -> RuleQueue: enqueueForTellNext(ALARM, "Alarm Cleared")
    end
    Profile -> Profile: currentAlarm = null
  end
end
Profile -> PG: optional save rule_node_state
Profile -> Actor: tellSuccess(original telemetry/attribute)
deactivate Profile
deactivate Actor

== External root clear updates Device Profile state ==
RuleQueue -> Actor: TbMsgType.ALARM_CLEAR
activate Actor
Actor -> Profile: onMsg(ctx,msg)
activate Profile
Profile -> Profile: DeviceState.processAlarmClearNotification\nmatch AlarmId, currentAlarm=null\nclear create-rule state
Profile -> PG: optional save rule_node_state
Profile -> Actor: tellSuccess(root action)
deactivate Profile
deactivate Actor

== Edge uplink clear ==
actor "Source Edge" as SourceEdge
participant "EdgeGrpcSession" as EdgeGrpc
participant "AlarmEdgeProcessor" as EdgeProcessor
participant "BaseAlarmProcessor" as BaseProcessor
queue "Other related Edge events" as OtherEdges

SourceEdge -> EdgeGrpc: UplinkMsg ALARM_CLEAR_RPC_MESSAGE
activate EdgeGrpc
EdgeGrpc -> EdgeProcessor: processAlarmMsgFromEdge(tenant,edge,msg)
activate EdgeProcessor
EdgeProcessor -> EdgeProcessor: source EdgeId ThreadLocal = edge
EdgeProcessor -> BaseProcessor: processAlarmMsg(...)
activate BaseProcessor
BaseProcessor -> Service: findAlarmById; clearAlarm directly
Service -> PG: clear_alarm(...)
PG --> Service: first or duplicate result
Service -> EdgeEvent: ActionEntityEvent(ALARM_CLEAR)\nsource EdgeId from ThreadLocal
EdgeEvent -> RuleQueue: Edge notification
RuleQueue -> OtherEdges: save events for related Edges\nexcluding source Edge
Service --> BaseProcessor: result
BaseProcessor --> EdgeProcessor: immediate Future success
deactivate BaseProcessor
EdgeProcessor -> EdgeProcessor: remove ThreadLocal
EdgeProcessor --> EdgeGrpc: success
deactivate EdgeProcessor
EdgeGrpc --> SourceEdge: uplink response success
deactivate EdgeGrpc

note over SourceEdge,Profile
This Edge branch bypasses DefaultAlarmSubscriptionService and
EntityActionService: no local WS, AlarmTrigger or root ALARM_CLEAR.
end note

== Concurrent duplicate clear and ACK comparison ==
participant "Clear A" as A
participant "Clear B" as B
participant "ACK C" as C
A -> PG: SELECT alarm FOR UPDATE
PG --> A: lock granted
B -> PG: SELECT same alarm FOR UPDATE
note over B,PG: waits for A
A -> PG: UPDATE cleared=true, clear_ts=A
A --> PG: commit
PG --> B: refreshed row already cleared
B -> PG: no UPDATE; return cleared=false
C -> PG: SELECT same row FOR UPDATE
PG --> C: cleared=true acknowledged=false
C -> PG: UPDATE acknowledged=true, ack_ts=C
C --> PG: final status CLEARED_ACK

@enduml
